-  "ideal_answer": "**THE GRYFFINDOR LAW FIRM P.C.**\n\nHarry Potter, Esq.\n\nRonald Weasley, Esq.\n\nHermione Granger, Esq.\n\n13 Hogwarts Way\n\nLondon, New Jersey 07006\n\nPhone: (973) 131-3113\n\nFax: (973) 111-3333\n\n*Attorneys for Defendant Firebolt USA, LLC*\n\n**IN THE UNITED STATES DISTRICT COURT**\n\n**FOR THE DISTRICT OF NEW JERSEY**\n\n<table style=\"width:43%;\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 42%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><p>DRACO MALFOY, VINCENT CRABBE and GREG GOYLE, individually and on behalf of all others similarly situated,</p>\n<p>Plaintiffs,</p>\n<p>-against-</p>\n<p>FIREBOLT USA, LLC,</p>\n<p>Defendant.</p></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n> No: 25-cv-1234-DMC-MF\n\n**[DEFENDANT FIREBOLT USA, LLC'S RESPONSE TO PLAINTIFFS' FIRST REQUEST FOR THE PRODUCTION OF DOCUMENTS]{.underline}**\n\nPursuant to Rules 26 and 34 of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure and Local Civil Rule 34.1, Defendant Firebolt USA, LLC (\"Defendant\" or \"Firebolt\"), by its undersigned counsel, hereby responds and objects as follows to Plaintiffs' First Request for the Production of Documents to Defendant Firebolt USA, LLC as follows:\n\n**[GENERAL OBJECTIONS]{.underline}**\n\nThe following general objections apply to each separate interrogatory (\"Request\") and are incorporated by this reference, to the extent applicable, into each specific response, as if set forth in full in each numbered response.\n\n1.  Firebolt has based its responses to each Request on the assumption that Plaintiffs, in propounding these Requests, did not intend to seek information protected against discovery by the attorney-client privilege, the work product doctrine, the joint defense privilege, or any other judicially recognized privileges or protections. To the extent that any Requests are intended to elicit such information, Firebolt objects to them and asserts all applicable privileges and protections to the fullest extent permitted by law. If any information is inadvertently disclosed in response to these Requests that is properly the subject of any applicable privilege or protection, such inadvertent disclosure is not to be construed as a waiver of such privilege or protection.\n\n2.  Firebolt objects to each and every Request to the extent it seeks disclosure of information where such disclosure would violate any constitutional, statutory, or common law privacy right of any individual or entity; confidentiality agreement between Firebolt and any individual; confidentiality of settlement discussions or agreements; or court order restricting the disclosure of information.\n\n3.  In responding to Plaintiffs' Requests, Firebolt does not in any way intend to waive, but rather preserves, the right to object on any ground as to:\n\n> a\\. competency, relevancy, materiality and admissibility;\n>\n> b\\. the use of any of the responses in any subsequent proceedings, including the\n>\n> trial of this or any other action; and\n>\n> c\\. any further Requests or other discovery.\n\n4.  Firebolt objects to each and every Request to the extent it seeks information beyond the scope of discovery contemplated by Rule 26(b) of the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure.\n\n5.  Firebolt objects to each and every Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt or to the extent it seeks information not in Firebolt's possession, custody, or control. Firebolt specifically objects to Plaintiffs' definitions of \"you,\" \"your,\" and \"Firebolt,\" and other definitions and Requests using those terms, to the extent they seek information from any entity other than Firebolt because inclusion of other entities besides Firebolt renders such definitions overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive and impermissibly seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, and control. Accordingly, all responses herein are made by and on behalf of Firebolt alone and no other entity or person.\n\n6.  Firebolt also objects to each and every Request to the extent it seeks information from former employees, directors, and others who are no longer under the employment, or act on behalf of, or act at the direction of, Firebolt. Moreover, because the definitions of these terms include attorneys, accountants, and other representatives and agents, Firebolt objects to these definitions to the extent these terms can be interpreted to seek information protected against discovery by the attorney-client privilege, the work product doctrine, the joint defense privilege, or any other judicially recognized privilege or protection. Firebolt asserts all applicable privileges and protections to the fullest extent permitted by law.\n\n7.  Firebolt objects to the defined term \"Rims,\" and other definitions and Requests using that term, as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence, and to the extent it impermissibly seeks information not in Firebolt's possession, custody, or control. Among other things, Firebolt does not design, manufacture, install, or replace vehicle parts.\n\n8.  Firebolt objects to the defined term \"Relevant Time Period\" and other definitions and Requests using that term, as vague, ambiguous, arbitrary and overbroad rendering the term and Requests using it unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence because, among other things, it seeks information beyond the scope of the alleged class period.\n\n9.  Firebolt objects to each and every Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that each such Request is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\n10. Firebolt's responses to Plaintiffs' Requests have been prepared according to the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure pursuant to a reasonable and duly diligent investigation and search for responsive information and documents. To the extent that these Requests purport to require more, Firebolt objects because (i) the requests would exceed the scope of permissible discovery contemplated by the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure; and (ii) compliance with the requests as phrased would be oppressive, harassing, and unduly burdensome.\n\n11. Firebolt objects to each and every Request to the extent that it calls for disclosure of trade secrets or other confidential research, development, commercial or proprietary information. To the extent that such information is relevant to the subject matter of this litigation, and no objection otherwise has been asserted, Firebolt will provide such information subject to the provisions of the parties' stipulated protective order entered in this case on December 1, 2025.\n\n12. By submitting these responses, Firebolt does not in any way adopt Plaintiffs' purported definitions of words and phrases contained in Plaintiffs' Requests. Firebolt objects to those definitions to the extent that they are inconsistent with the ordinary and customary meaning of such words and phrases. Likewise, Firebolt objects to Plaintiffs' purported definitions to the extent that they purport to impose upon Firebolt any obligations broader than, or inconsistent with, applicable discovery rules or common law.\n\n13. Firebolt has not yet completed its investigation of the facts related to this litigation. Consequently, all of the responses contained herein are based only on such information and documentation that is presently available to Firebolt and disclose only the information and contentions presently known to Firebolt. Firebolt reserves the right to amend these responses, and to offer related evidence, as additional facts are ascertained, analyses are made, research is completed, and contentions become apparent.\n\n**[SPECIFIC RESPONSES AND OBJECTIONS TO REQUESTS FOR PRODUCTION]{.underline}**\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 1:**\n\n> All documents concerning Plaintiffs, any of Plaintiffs' Vehicles, or any of Plaintiffs' Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 1:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Plaintiffs,\" ''Vehicles\" and \"Rims\" as overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defects at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Firebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt agrees to produce the following documents responsive to this Request for the named Plaintiffs' vehicles: work orders/service records/warranty histories, Service and Warranty Information booklets (including New Vehicle Limited Warranty), Service and Warranty Information/Certified Pre-Owned Limited Warranty, Owner's Manuals, New Car Brochures, First Class Tire and Wheel Coverage brochures, correspondence, and dealer documents.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 2:**\n\nAll documents concerning Plaintiffs' purchases or leases of their Vehicles.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 2:**\n\n> *See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 3:**\n\n> All documents concerning Plaintiffs' purchase, replacement, or repair of any of their Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 3:**\n\n> *See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1.\n\nBy way of further response, Firebolt would normally not be in possession of documents concerning Plaintiffs' replacement or repair of Rims if performed by other than Firebolt dealer.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 4:**\n\nAll documents that Firebolt provided to Plaintiffs in connection with their acquisition of any Vehicles, including any contracts, warranties, guarantees, promises of repair, replacement, or refund, whether such documents were provided to Plaintiffs in hard-copy form and/or made available via Firebolt's website, or by any other method of dissemination.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 4:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms and phrases \"Firebolt,\" \"Plaintiffs,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"provided to,\" \"in connection with,\" \"acquisition,\" \"contracts,\" \"guarantees,\" \"promises of repair, replacement, or refund\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Requests Nos. 1-3.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 6:**\n\nAll documents provided to Plaintiffs in connection with their acquisition of any Rims, including any contracts, warranties, guarantees, promises of repair, replacement, or refund, whether such documents were provided to Plaintiffs in hard-copy form and/or made available via Firebolt's website, or by any other method of dissemination.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 5:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the tem1s and phrases \"Firebolt,\" \"Rims,\" \"provided to,\" \"in connection with,\" \"acquisition,\" \"contracts,\" \"guarantees,\" \"promises of repair, replacement, or refund\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request Nos. 1, 4.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 6:**\n\nAll documents concerning all terms and conditions, disclaimers, or other exclusions that you contend are applicable to Plaintiffs' Vehicles or Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 6:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Vehicles,\" \"Rims,\" \"terms,\" \"conditions,\" \"disclaimers,\" and \"other exclusions\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1 and, specifically, the applicable warranties produced in response thereto.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 7:**\n\nAll documents evidencing or concerning any communication between Firebolt and any of the Plaintiffs, including communications concerning any of Plaintiffs' Vehicles or Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 7:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Plaintiffs,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"Rims,\" \"any communication,\" \"Firebolt\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation that Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1, specifically, documents pertaining to named Plaintiffs' vehicles.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 8:**\n\nAll documents concerning repairs performed by Firebolt to any of Plaintiffs' Vehicles or Rims including any repair or replacement of any of Plaintiffs' Rims. This request includes all documents evidencing Firebolt's statements or suggestions that any of the Rims on Plaintiffs' Vehicles were damaged or bent in any way, even if Plaintiffs did not repair or replace the Rims or chose not to have the repair or replacement completed.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 8:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Plaintiffs,'' \"Vehicles,\" \"Rims,\" \"repairs,\" \"replacement,\" \"statements,\" \"suggestions,\" \"damaged,\" and \"bent\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking infom1ation outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request Nos. 1, 7.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 9:**\n\nAll Vehicle Data Files and/or records of all sales and leases of Vehicles, including the identities of all purchasers and lessees and prices paid.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 9:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Vehicles,\" \"Vehicle Data Files,\" \"records,\" \"sales,\" \"leases,\" and \"prices paid\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 10:**\n\n> Any TSB concerning the Vehicles.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 10:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"TSB\" and \"Vehicles\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt' s possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 11, *infra*.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 11:**\n\n> Any TSB concerning the Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 11:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"TSB\" and \"Rims\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt agrees to produce materials responsive to this Request in its possession, custody, or control.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 12:**\n\nAll documents concerning, describing or otherwise referring to any replacement items or parts provided by defendant or its agent to Plaintiffs for Plaintiffs' Vehicles or Rims, whether such parts were provided without further charge to Plaintiffs or otherwise.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 12:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms and phrases \"describing,\" \"referring,\" \"replacement items or parts,\" \"provided,\" \"defendant,\" \"agent,\" \"Plaintiffs,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"Rims,\" and \"further charge\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the pem1issible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request on the grounds that it violates the privacy rights of consumers protected under state and federal law. In addition to violations of applicable laws, this Request also calls for disclosure of information that Firebolt customers have an expectation Firebolt will keep private.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request Nos. 1, 7.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 13:**\n\nAll documents concerning any investigation, survey, or study related to the Rims, whether such investigation, survey, or study was done by Firebolt, a different manufacturer or supplier of the Rims, or by a paid or unpaid consultant or other outsider.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 13:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"investigation,\" \"survey,\" \"study,\" \"Rims,\" \"Firebolt,\" \"different manufacturer or supplier,\" \"consultant,\" and \"outsider\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Among other things, Firebolt does not design, manufacture, repair, replace, equip, or install vehicle parts/components.\n\nFirebolt also objects to the extent this Request seeks confidential information or information covered by the attorney-client privilege, the work product doctrine, business and trade secret privileges, or any other privileges or immunities from discovery authorized by law.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt does not design or manufacture vehicles or vehicle parts/components. Firebolt's discovery efforts are ongoing, and Firebolt reserves the right to supplement its responses if responsive materials are found.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 14:**\n\nAll documents concerning any investigation, survey, or study related to the 16-inch Rims, whether such investigation, survey, or study was done by Firebolt, a different manufacturer or supplier of the Rims, or by a paid or unpaid consultant or other outsider, without regard to the Relevant Time Period.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 14:**\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 13. Firebolt further objects to this Request because \"16-inch Rims\" are not at issue in this action and as such the Request is overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 15:**\n\nAll documents concerning or analyzing whether Firebolt should recall or repair all or some Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 15:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the term \"analyzing,\" \"Firebolt,\" \"Rims,\" \"recall,\" and \"repair\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses