ting forth,\" \"describing,\" \"explaining,\" \"projecting,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"potentially,\" \"actually,\" \"affected by,\" \"exhibiting,\" \"potentially exhibiting,\" \"problem\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Among other things, Firebolt does not design or manufacture vehicles or design, manufacture, repair, replace, equip, or install vehicle parts/components.\n\nFirebolt also objects to the extent this Request seeks confidential information or information covered by the attorney-client privilege, the work product doctrine, business and trade secret privileges, or any other privileges or immunities from discovery authorized by law.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt has conducted a reasonable and diligent search and has found no responsive documents.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 41:**\n\nAll communications or records of communications with (i.e., to and/or from) any governmental agency (including the National Highway Transportation Safety Administration or any other agency, state or federal) concerning the Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 41:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the term \"Rims\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Firebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt has conducted a reasonable and diligent search and, as it understands this Request, has found no responsive documents.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 42:**\n\nAll communications or records of communications with (i.e., to and/or from) any governmental agency (including the National Highway Transportation Safety Administration or any other agency, state or federal) concerning the Vehicles equipped with the Rims or the Rims in conjunction with low profile tires or other components of the Vehicles in anyway.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 42:**\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 41.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 43:**\n\nAll communications issued by Firebolt to the public and/or to Firebolt customers concerning problems or defects, realized or potential, in the Rims or in the Vehicles relating to the Rims, including press releases, website postings, advertisements, written or electronic communications, or statements in Firebolt's financial reports.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 43:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Firebolt,\" \"public,\" \"problems,\" \"defects,\" \"realized or potential,\" \"Rims,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"press releases,\" \"website postings,\" \"advertisements,\" \"written or electronic communications,\" \"statements,\" and \"financial reports\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1. Firebolt further responds that after a diligent search, Firebolt has found no press releases, website postings, advertisements, statements in financial reports or other communications to the public generally relating to \"problems or defects\" with the Rims. With respect to communications with individual customers about the Rims, please see Response and Objections to Request No. 30.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 44:**\n\nAll documents concerning the extension of warranties or any potential extension of warranties covering the Rims. This includes, but is not limited to, all communications to Firebolt customers regarding the extension of warranties covering the Vehicles or Rims, as well as any documents concerning Firebolt's decision to extend or not to extend the warranties.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 44:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"extension,\" \"extend,\" \"potential extension,\" \"Firebolt,\" \"Rims\" and \"Vehicles\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing general and. specific objections, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\nFirebolt has conducted a reasonable and diligent search and has found no responsive documents.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 45:**\n\nAll documents concerning the repair or replacement of Rims, whether such replacement was with original equipment or not, for any customer where such repair or replacement was not covered by any warranty.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 45:**\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request Nos. 1, 7, 30, and 33.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 46:**\n\nAll corporate organizational charts for defendant for the period 2001-2011, and all documents sufficient to identify all foreign and domestic predecessors, successors, parents, subsidiaries, divisions, affiliates and sister companies of Firebolt that have been involved in the design, production, specification, performance, testing and/or manufacture of the Rims.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 46:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"foreign,\" \"predecessors,\" \"successors,\" \"parents,\" \"subsidiaries,\" \"divisions,\" \"affiliates,\" \"sister companies,\" \"Firebolt,\" \"design,\" ·\"production,\" \"specification,\" \"performance,\" \"testing,\" and \"manufacture\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Among other things, Firebolt does not design or manufacture vehicles or desi6rn, manufacture, repair, replace, equip, or install vehicle parts/components.\n\nFirebolt also objects to the extent this Request seeks confidential information or information covered by the attorney-client privilege, the work product doctrine, business and trade secret privileges, or any other privileges or immunities from discovery authorized by law.\n\nSubject to and without waiving the foregoing objections, Firebolt further states that it is a subsidiary of Quidditch North America Corporation, which in turn is a subsidiary of Quidditch AG.\n\n**REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 47:**\n\nAll documents concerning advertisements or promotions of the Vehicles or Rims, including but not limited to brochures, internet postings, direct-mail advertisements, advertisements by electronic mail, scripts for television advertisements, and magazine or newspaper publications for the years 2015 through the present.\n\n**RESPONSE TO REQUEST FOR PRODUCTION NO. 47:**\n\nFirebolt incorporates the general objections stated above as though set forth fully in this response and also specifically objects to this Request as follows: Firebolt objects to this Request and the terms \"Rims,\" \"Vehicles,\" \"advertisements,\" \"promotions,\" \"brochures,\" \"internet postings,\" \"direct-mail advertisements by electronic mail,\" \"scripts,\" \"television,\" \"magazine,\" \"newspaper,\" and \"2015 through present\" as vague, ambiguous, overbroad, unduly burdensome, harassing, oppressive, and seeking information outside the permissible scope of discovery, unrelated to the claims or defenses of the parties or to the alleged defect at issue in this case, and thus not reasonably calculated to lead to the discovery of admissible evidence.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent it seeks to require Firebolt to respond on behalf of any entity other than Firebolt and to the extent it seeks information not within Firebolt's possession, custody, or control and/or concerns transactions not involving Firebolt. Among other things, Firebolt does not design or manufacture vehicles or design, manufacture, repair, replace, equip, or install vehicle parts/components.\n\nFirebolt further objects to this Request to the extent that it seeks information presumptively within the custody or control of Plaintiffs or in the public domain on the grounds that it is unduly burdensome, harassing, and oppressive.\n\nSubject to and without waiver of the foregoing general and specific objection, Firebolt responds as follows:\n\n*See* Firebolt's Response and Objections to Request No. 1.\n\n<table>\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 91%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 8%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><p>Dated: February __, 2026</p>\n<table style=\"width:48%;\">\n<colgroup>\n<col style=\"width: 17%\" />\n<col style=\"width: 30%\" />\n</colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Respectfully submitted,</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td><p>____________________</p>\n<p>Harry Potter, Esq.</p>\n<p>Ron Weasley, Esq.</p>\n<p>Hermione Granger, Esq.</p>\n<p>The Gryffindor Law Firm</p>\n<p>13 Hogwarts Way</p>\n<p>London, New Jersey 07006</p>\n<p>Tel: (973) 131-3113</p>\n<p>Fax: (973) 111-3333</p>\n<p>hpotter@gryffindorlaw.com</p>\n<p><a href=\"mailto:rweasley@gryffindorlaw.com\">rweasley@gryffindorlaw.com</a></p>\n<p>hgranger@gryffindorlaw.com</p>\n<p><em>Attorneys for Defendant Firebolt USA, LLC</em></p></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
